===================================================================
CLASSIFICATION SUMMARY
===================================================================
A) Browser network-log artifacts ("Failed to load resource", NOT JS console.error()):
   - PUT  /api/settings/crash-report        -> 405 (x2: OptIn enable, settings toggle)
   - GET  /api/crash/pending                -> 404 (bugs tab)
   - GET  /api/feedback-hub notices         -> failed (notices tab)
   - GET  /api/crash/<id>/prefill-url       -> 404 (sample preview; by design)
   ROOT CAUSE: stale uvicorn (PID 59028) predates this branch. Live /openapi.json
   registers ZERO crash/feedback/notice routes; source apps/api/main.py includes
   all of them (lines 252-256). 405 (not 404) for PUT because unmatched request
   falls through to the SPA StaticFiles mount (GET/HEAD only).

B) GENUINE JS console.error() calls:
   - "[BugReportTab] load failed: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'code')"
     Source: BugReportTab.svelte:43 (catch) logging a TypeError thrown by
     apps/web/src/lib/api/client.ts:57-58 which assumes every non-2xx JSON body
     has an {error:{code,...}} envelope. FastAPI HTTPException/404/405/422 bodies
     are {"detail": ...} -> body.error is undefined -> err.code throws.
     NOTE: crash router raises HTTPException(404) for unknown ids (crash.py:288),
     and the app's custom handler (main.py:225) only wraps AppError, NOT
     HTTPException -> this bug is reproducible on a FRESH backend too, not only stale.
